&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.2;&quot;&gt;At Flo, we empower women across the world to improve their health and well-being with an unmatched user experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;We are obsessed with understanding the needs of our users, we work in partnership with analysts and user researchers to uncover the ‘why’ and ensure the very best product gets built.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.2;&quot;&gt;From launching new features to delivering seamless end-to-end journeys, we’re looking for passionate individuals with a growth mindset who can innovate, experiment and move fast.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Become our QA Release Manager and help us smoothly deliver content to the Flo app. Your main objective will be to create and test content within the content management tools, ensuring it is delivered to the audience bug-free.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join one of our cross-functional engineering teams while becoming an integral part of our larger QA release management community. You will have the opportunity to contribute to and shape best practices and quality assurance standards, ensuring excellence across our projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.2;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Content delivery management (delivering and supporting the content by using the internal content management tools);&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manual testing of the new features together with content provided in the app;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bug detection and making bug reports in Jira;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-team communication and assistance in solving cross-team issues (content, designer, support, dev);&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working in an Agile and fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
