&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;500M+ downloads. 80M+ monthly users. A decade of building – and we’re still accelerating.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flo is the world’s #1 health &amp;amp; fitness app worldwide on a mission to build a better future for female health. Backed by a $200M investment led by General Atlantic, we became the first product of our kind to reach a $1B valuation in 2024 – and we’re not slowing down.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With 7M paid subscribers and the highest-rated experience in the App Store’s health category, we’ve spent 10 years earning trust at scale. Now, we’re building the next generation of digital health – AI-powered, privacy-first, clinically backed – to help our users know their body better.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Senior Technical Product Manager to join our Health Records &amp;amp; Virtual Clinics team. This team is building the foundational infrastructure that powers Flo’s next generation of personalised healthcare experiences. Our mission is to integrate diverse health data sources, from clinical systems and external vendors to user-reported data, including data from wearables directly or via Health Connect/HealthKit into a unified, reliable, and actionable health record. This foundation will enable a new Virtual Clinics direction, delivering personalised, data-driven care journeys at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While this is a deeply technical and data-heavy area, we believe that the true value of health data is unlocked through intuitive, trustworthy, and beautifully designed user experiences. You will partner closely with product design to ensure complex, fragmented health data is translated into clear, intuitive, and user-friendly experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in product management, including experience in platform, data, or infrastructure products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical background, with experience working on APIs, data pipelines, or distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating third-party vendors, APIs, or complex ecosystems (healthcare experience is a strong plus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of data modeling, data quality challenges, and trade-offs in building scalable data platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven passion for building high-quality user experiences, with a track record of partnering closely with design to ship intuitive and elegant products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate complex technical systems and data into simple, user-friendly interfaces and flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in regulated environments and collaborating with clinical, legal, privacy, and security stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to define and deliver products in ambiguous, fast-moving environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical mindset, with experience defining and tracking metrics for platform/data products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of iterative delivery and experimentation, even within complex technical domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent stakeholder management and communication skills, with the ability to align cross-functional teams around complex initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for building impactful healthcare products and improving user outcomes through data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll be responsible for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute the product strategy and roadmap for Health Records and data integrations, enabling scalable and secure ingestion of data from multiple vendors and systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end lifecycle of health data: from ingestion and normalization to enrichment and activation in downstream experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the development of a unified health data model that supports personalised user experiences, clinical use cases, and Virtual Clinics services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with design team to creation of best-in-class UI/UX patterns for surfacing health insights, longitudinal records, and care journeys&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that health data is presented in a way that is actionable, empathetic, and clinically responsible, balancing simplicity with accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Engineering, Data, Clinical, and Legal teams to ensure data accuracy, regulatory compliance, and user privacy. Own the creation of well-scoped product and technical specifications, and actively participate in technical trade-off discussions. Given the tech- and infrastructure-heavy nature of the team, operate as a deeply embedded partner within the squad, not just a stakeholder, contributing to architecture-level decisions and day-to-day execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive vendor integration strategy, including prioritisation, evaluation, and long-term partnership management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with AI Platform team to ensure high-quality structured data is available for models and personalised insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance speed and scalability, making high-judgment trade-offs across infrastructure, data quality, and user-facing impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish metrics to evaluate data quality, coverage, and downstream impact on user outcomes and business goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay on top of industry trends in digital health, interoperability, and virtual care, as well as evolving UX patterns in consumer health products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#LI-Hybrid #LI-AJ1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range - London - gross per year (ranges may vary based on skills and experience)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£91,600&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£115,000 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range - Vilnius - gross per month (ranges may vary based on skills and experience)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€7.300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€8.800 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a mission-led, product-driven team. We move fast, stay focused and take ownership – from brief to build to impact. Debate is encouraged. Decisions are shared. We care about craft, ship with purpose, and always raise the bar.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be working with people who take their work seriously, not themselves. It takes commitment, resilience, and the drive to keep going when things get tough. Because better health outcomes are worth it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll get&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We support impact with meaningful reward. Here’s what that looks like:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and annual reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to participate in Flo’s performance incentive scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid holiday, sick leave, and female health leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced parental leave and pay for maternity, paternity, same-sex and adoptive parents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accelerated professional growth through world-changing work and learning support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-person collaboration and work in a hybrid model, with 3 days per week spent in the office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-week fully paid sabbatical at 5-year Floversary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flo Premium for friends &amp;amp; family, plus more health, pension and wellbeing perks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, equity and inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our strength is in our differences. At Flo, hiring is based on merit, skill and what you bring to the role – nothing else. We’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds, communities and identities. Read our &lt;a href=&quot;https://flo.health/privacy-policy-for-job-applicants&quot;&gt;privacy notice for job applicants&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
